COMPANY CONTEXT

Elip (tryelip.ai) is an early-stage YC startup building an AI job agent that lives in WhatsApp. Job seekers message the agent their requirements (role, location, experience) in plain language; the agent scans [~16 million] job postings daily and sends back a small number of curated matches — typically 3 — each with an honest "catch" (real downsides like long commute or startup chaos), instead of the spam-wall experience of job portals. The product is free for job seekers; [employers pay per hire]. No app, no signup friction — the entire experience is a WhatsApp chat.

Target users: Indian students and early-career professionals (0–5 years experience), especially tech, across metro and tier-2 cities. Core user pain: the broken hiring process — ghost job listings, ATS black holes, recruiter ghosting, hundreds of applications with zero replies.

Brand voice: witty, irreverent, anti-broken-hiring, meme-literate, talks like a hostel friend, never corporate. The villain is the broken hiring system; Elip is the effortless alternative.

